# Persona 2: Batsu (SLPS-02785): the codes this game adds to Persona 2: Tsumi's table.
# The two games keep the same 12x12 font in memory up to glyph 0x0A0E, so the entry lists
# tables/ps1/SLPS-02100.tbl first and this file after it. This file holds only the glyphs from 0x0A0F that
# this game's font adds. 16-bit little-endian glyph numbers, keys in memory byte order.
# Read from the font by eye, then proofread against the disc as Tsumi's table was: every message was decoded and
# each code checked in the words around it, beside the enlarged glyph.
# 258 kanji, 3 kana and 14 marks are listed. Left out on purpose, so they read as U+FFFD: 12 of these codes the
# script uses that stayed in doubt (21 uses on the disc), and the glyphs no message uses.
# Listed last, as a space: the three control words that only leave a gap in the line (0x1130, 0x1131, 0x1132; in
# Tsumi they are 0x111F to 0x1121). The layout's cleanup takes the indent they make at a line's start off again.
